WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:15.716
Zann realized this wormhole, too, was on the ground.

2
00:00:16.276 --> 00:00:21.017
He yanked on the edge of the wormhole as hard as he could, propelling himself upward.

3
00:00:21.637 --> 00:00:26.479
He flew out and landed on his feet, but he forgot that Perda was still shackled to him.

4
00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:28.840
"Hey!" she cried.

5
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:35.210
"Whoa!" She crashed into Zann, and the two of them collapsed on the ground in a tangle of

6
00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.090
arms and legs.

7
00:00:36.991 --> 00:00:38.771
Zing landed on Zann's face.

8
00:00:38.791 --> 00:00:45.154
"Oof!" Zann grunted, embarrassed to realize that his elbow was in Perda's ear.

9
00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:47.395
Perda quickly snapped her fingers.

10
00:00:47.895 --> 00:00:50.716
"Unshackle," she said, undoing the spell.

11
00:00:51.316 --> 00:00:53.577
She jumped to her feet and looked around.

12
00:00:53.597 --> 00:00:55.658
"I wonder where we are?"

13
00:00:56.498 --> 00:01:01.256
Zann glanced back just in time to see the wormhole swirl shut and disappear.

14
00:01:01.816 --> 00:01:03.777
He also realized his arm hurt.

15
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:07.298
"Ow," he said, noticing a scrape.

16
00:01:07.318 --> 00:01:09.619
"I think I landed on a rock."

17
00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:12.580
He unshackled himself from Zing.

18
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.981
Then he snapped his fingers and touched the wound on his arm to perform a simple Healing spell.

19
00:01:19.602 --> 00:01:20.722
But nothing happened.

20
00:01:21.362 --> 00:01:24.943
The scrape still stung, and it still looked red and raw.

21
00:01:24.963 --> 00:01:26.144
"What's wrong?"

22
00:01:26.524 --> 00:01:27.164
Perda asked.

23
00:01:27.744 --> 00:01:30.527
Zann rubbed his hands together to create more friction.

24
00:01:31.147 --> 00:01:32.328
Then he tried again.

25
00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:34.250
"My Healing spell isn't working!"

26
00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.270
he exclaimed.

27
00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:38.313
"What if we did land in that no-magic world again?"

28
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:42.376
"This doesn't look anything like that world," Perda said.

29
00:01:42.396 --> 00:01:46.760
"It's probably not working because the vortex sapped your energy.

30
00:01:47.461 --> 00:01:50.383
You should rest and then try again in a few minutes."

31
00:01:51.124 --> 00:01:51.924
Zann nodded.

32
00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.306
"I hope she's right," he thought.

33
00:01:54.326 --> 00:01:56.128
"My arm doesn't hurt that much.

34
00:01:56.696 --> 00:01:59.297
But I do not want to be stuck in a world without magic!"

35
00:01:59.977 --> 00:02:02.057
To distract himself, he looked around.

36
00:02:02.578 --> 00:02:07.199
The land was just as flat and colorless as it had appeared from the vortex.

37
00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:12.180
Now that he could see more, though, Zann spotted mountains rising in the distance.

38
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.682
He also saw a crooked, weak-looking sapling growing very close to where the wormhole had been.

39
00:02:19.282 --> 00:02:24.704
It cast only a few jagged slivers of shade that didn't do much to combat the heat of

40
00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:25.784
the blazing sun.

41
00:02:26.496 --> 00:02:27.236
"Look over here."

42
00:02:27.936 --> 00:02:29.997
Perda had wandered a short distance away.

43
00:02:30.597 --> 00:02:34.098
She was staring down at some limp greenish gray sprouts.

44
00:02:34.798 --> 00:02:36.959
"This looks like some kind of garden.

45
00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:40.180
See? These plants are growing in rows."

46
00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.321
"That means there must be people nearby."

47
00:02:43.001 --> 00:02:45.361
Zann noticed a shallow hole in the ground.

48
00:02:46.362 --> 00:02:50.023
A crude stone shovel with a wooden handle was lying next to it.

49
00:02:50.043 --> 00:02:52.103
"Look, they left one of their tools."

50
00:02:52.864 --> 00:02:54.204
Perda walked over to look.

51
00:02:55.032 --> 00:02:57.913
"Someone dug this hole recently," she said.

52
00:02:57.933 --> 00:03:03.776
"See? The dirt on the shovel is still a little damp, even though the air here is really

53
00:03:03.856 --> 00:03:07.617
dry." Zann was impressed that she'd noticed something like that.

54
00:03:08.158 --> 00:03:11.019
Perda really was one of the smartest people he knew.

55
00:03:11.679 --> 00:03:16.281
She would make a great researcher someday, if that was what she decided to do for a career.

56
00:03:16.301 --> 00:03:18.882
"I wonder where they went," he said.

57
00:03:19.462 --> 00:03:23.224
Then he noticed Zing creeping toward a patch of thorny bushes.

58
00:03:23.992 --> 00:03:26.153
"Hey Zing, don't you dare start chasing something!

59
00:03:26.714 --> 00:03:28.275
That's what got us into this mess, remember?"

60
00:03:29.755 --> 00:03:31.196
He grabbed the dragon's leash.

61
00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:36.699
Zing opened his mouth as if to shoot flames at him, but only a little steam came out.

62
00:03:36.719 --> 00:03:38.741
"Uh-oh," Zann said.

63
00:03:38.761 --> 00:03:40.802
"Zing's magic isn't working either.

64
00:03:41.322 --> 00:03:42.303
That's a bad sign."

65
00:03:43.123 --> 00:03:45.024
For a second, Perda looked worried.

66
00:03:45.584 --> 00:03:47.345
Then her expression brightened.

67
00:03:47.365 --> 00:03:51.508
"Wait—we undid our Shackle spells after we got here, remember?

68
00:03:52.032 --> 00:03:54.633
That means there's at least some magic energy.

69
00:03:55.353 --> 00:03:57.054
It just must be really weak.

70
00:03:57.734 --> 00:04:00.495
Or maybe it works differently here than it does in Magica."

71
00:04:01.216 --> 00:04:03.177
Once again Zann was impressed.

72
00:04:03.737 --> 00:04:08.879
Before he could respond, Zing yanked on his leash, which made Zann's arm hurt again.

73
00:04:08.899 --> 00:04:11.020
"Ouch," he complained.

74
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.580
"What are you—oh!"

75
00:04:13.841 --> 00:04:17.342
A girl stepped into view from behind the shrub Zing was watching.

76
00:04:17.882 --> 00:04:21.464
She was about their age, with reddish brown hair and a few freckles.

77
00:04:22.196 --> 00:04:25.858
She was dressed in a drab, simple outfit of rough-looking cloth.

78
00:04:25.878 --> 00:04:29.819
"Hello," she said, her voice shaking a little.

79
00:04:29.839 --> 00:04:31.600
"Where did you come from?

80
00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:37.882
One moment I was alone, and then Her voice trailed off uncertainly.

81
00:04:37.902 --> 00:04:41.684
"I'm Perda, and this is Zann," Perda said.

82
00:04:41.704 --> 00:04:42.884
"What's your name?"

83
00:04:42.904 --> 00:04:45.345
"Mellis," the girl replied.

84
00:04:45.365 --> 00:04:47.586
"But where did you come from?"

85
00:04:47.606 --> 00:04:51.728
"We came through the vortex from a world called Magica," Zann said.

86
00:04:52.536 --> 00:04:54.237
Mellis blinked in confusion.

87
00:04:54.257 --> 00:04:57.498
"You came here from another world?"

88
00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.279
"Yes, that's right," Perda said.

89
00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:04.181
"Oh." Mellis looked as if she didn't believe them.

90
00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:05.801
But she didn't say so.

91
00:05:06.502 --> 00:05:12.224
Instead she said, "Well, wherever you came from, welcome to Terrica."

92
00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:15.465
"Terrica?" Perda looked thoughtful.

93
00:05:15.485 --> 00:05:20.527
"I don't remember seeing that world mentioned in any of your parents' books, Zann."

94
00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:22.088
Zann shrugged.

95
00:05:22.668 --> 00:05:25.889
"They say there are lots of worlds that haven't been discovered yet," he said.

96
00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:27.570
"I guess we just discovered one."

97
00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.392
He felt his arm throbbing and lifted it for a better look.

98
00:05:32.072 --> 00:05:33.492
Mellis noticed his scrape.

99
00:05:33.512 --> 00:05:35.493
"Oh, you're hurt!"

100
00:05:35.953 --> 00:05:36.594
she exclaimed.

101
00:05:36.614 --> 00:05:38.134
"I almost forgot."

102
00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:39.915
Perda stepped closer.

103
00:05:39.935 --> 00:05:42.696
"Our energy must be returning by now."

104
00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:47.398
She rubbed her hands together and touched the sore spot on Zann's arm.

105
00:05:47.978 --> 00:05:48.678
Nothing happened.

106
00:05:49.239 --> 00:05:52.240
She tried again, rubbing her hands on her legs this time.

107
00:05:53.084 --> 00:05:56.167
"Heal," she said as she touched the scrape again.

108
00:05:56.687 --> 00:05:58.048
Then she shook her head.

109
00:05:58.068 --> 00:06:02.692
"Still nothing—not even when I used a focusing word!"

110
00:06:02.712 --> 00:06:04.033
"Let's both try."

111
00:06:04.933 --> 00:06:09.417
Zann and Perda rubbed their hands together, and then both of them touched Zann's arm.

112
00:06:10.558 --> 00:06:14.040
But still the scrape remained, oozing a little bit of blood.

113
00:06:14.641 --> 00:06:16.082
Mellis looked perplexed.

114
00:06:16.822 --> 00:06:17.723
"What are you doing?"

115
00:06:18.223 --> 00:06:18.684
she asked.

116
00:06:19.364 --> 00:06:22.948
Zann tried to control the panic rising within him as he turned to her.

117
00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:27.434
Maybe Perda was right—maybe magic worked differently here.

118
00:06:27.454 --> 00:06:29.436
"Mellis," he said.

119
00:06:29.456 --> 00:06:31.799
"How does magic work here in Terrica?"

120
00:06:32.479 --> 00:06:34.101
Mellis blinked in confusion.

121
00:06:34.121 --> 00:06:36.624
"Magic?" she echoed.

122
00:06:36.644 --> 00:06:38.286
"What's that?"
